WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.781
landed in a rural area.

2
00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:18.143
The village was visible in the distance.

3
00:00:18.163 --> 00:00:22.826
"I see that ugly tower Zira added to her house," she thought.

4
00:00:23.327 --> 00:00:24.608
Then she looked around.

5
00:00:25.288 --> 00:00:27.310
She'd chosen her landing spot at random.

6
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.152
Now she had to find that plonk farm.

7
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.041
But she didn't even know what a plonk was!

8
00:00:33.881 --> 00:00:36.622
A woman was walking past with a basket under her arm.

9
00:00:37.922 --> 00:00:40.663
"Excuse me," Perda said, shuffling toward her.

10
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:43.343
"Is there a plonk farm around here?"

11
00:00:43.363 --> 00:00:45.184
"A plonk farm?"

12
00:00:45.684 --> 00:00:47.425
the woman asked in a friendly way.

13
00:00:48.185 --> 00:00:51.226
Then she saw Perda's shackled wrists and legs.

14
00:00:51.246 --> 00:00:53.446
"Oh dear," she said quickly.

15
00:00:54.006 --> 00:00:55.627
"You must be one of Zira's prisoners.

16
00:00:56.247 --> 00:00:58.268
If I help you, I might meet the same fate!

17
00:00:58.768 --> 00:00:59.448
I'm sorry."

18
00:01:00.224 --> 00:01:02.726
She hurried off before Perda could say anything else.

19
00:01:03.406 --> 00:01:04.807
Perda shuffled along the road.

20
00:01:05.327 --> 00:01:06.988
It was hard to walk in the shackles.

21
00:01:07.588 --> 00:01:09.069
She tried hopping instead.

22
00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.911
That was faster but much more tiring.

23
00:01:13.191 --> 00:01:14.252
A man came into sight.

24
00:01:14.932 --> 00:01:18.915
He was humming happily and juggling a loaf of bread and a couple of pieces of fruit.

25
00:01:18.935 --> 00:01:21.016
"Hello!" Perda said.

26
00:01:21.036 --> 00:01:24.418
"Could you please point me toward the nearest plonk farm?"

27
00:01:25.278 --> 00:01:30.389
The man was so surprised that he dropped the fruit, though he managed to hang onto the bread.

28
00:01:31.069 --> 00:01:31.749
"Who are you?"

29
00:01:32.129 --> 00:01:32.649
he asked.

30
00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:36.350
Then he, too, noticed the shackles and looked suspicious.

31
00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:39.431
"Why are you asking about the plonk farm?"

32
00:01:40.331 --> 00:01:45.053
Perda sighed, realizing it wouldn't be easy to find her friends if she was shackled.

33
00:01:45.653 --> 00:01:50.954
For a moment she was tempted to give up and zap back before Zira noticed she was missing.

34
00:01:51.594 --> 00:01:55.756
Zira would have to remove the shackles the next time she wanted Perda to do chores.

35
00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.777
Maybe then she could try to escape again.

36
00:01:59.397 --> 00:02:03.419
But then she noticed the man glancing nervously toward a side road.

37
00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:05.820
"Is that the way to the plonk farm?"

38
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:06.940
she blurted out.

39
00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.041
"You didn't hear it from me."

40
00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:14.143
The man quickly grabbed the fruit he'd dropped, hugging all his food to his chest.

41
00:02:14.163 --> 00:02:17.665
"I don't want Sir Vilkor to take back my stuff!"

42
00:02:18.625 --> 00:02:20.466
"You got that food from Vilkor?"

43
00:02:20.786 --> 00:02:21.466
Perda asked.

44
00:02:22.046 --> 00:02:25.708
"He should have told you that you can create all the food you want yourself."

45
00:02:26.664 --> 00:02:28.465
The man looked suspicious again.

46
00:02:28.485 --> 00:02:30.505
"What are you talking about?

47
00:02:31.265 --> 00:02:38.587
Sir Vilkor and his assistant, Zira, warned that troublemakers would be envious of their power and tell lies

48
00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:39.148
about them.

49
00:02:39.648 --> 00:02:41.748
Keep away from me, troublemaker!"

50
00:02:41.768 --> 00:02:45.129
"Wait!" Perda cried as he rushed away.

51
00:02:45.149 --> 00:02:48.330
"At least let me show you how you can—" "No!"

52
00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:49.830
the man snapped.

53
00:02:50.251 --> 00:02:54.972
"You're lucky I don't run back to the village and tell Sir Vilkor about your mischief!"

54
00:02:55.776 --> 00:02:56.937
Perda watched him go.

55
00:02:57.637 --> 00:03:03.040
Then she shuffled toward the side road, hoping she could find the plonk farm on her own.

56
00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:07.503
A few minutes later, she spotted a boy her age on the road ahead.

57
00:03:08.003 --> 00:03:09.384
She hopped to catch up to him.

58
00:03:09.404 --> 00:03:11.265
"Hi," she said.

59
00:03:11.285 --> 00:03:13.646
"Is there a plonk farm around here?"

60
00:03:14.687 --> 00:03:15.887
The boy stared at her.

61
00:03:15.907 --> 00:03:18.189
"Um, I don't know."

62
00:03:18.869 --> 00:03:20.930
His eyes were shifty and nervous.

63
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.612
"Please, don't worry," Perda said.

64
00:03:24.088 --> 00:03:25.789
"I won't tell anyone you spoke to me."

65
00:03:26.589 --> 00:03:28.090
She took a closer look at the boy.

66
00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:30.671
"Hmm, you look sort of familiar.

67
00:03:31.131 --> 00:03:31.911
Do I know you?"

68
00:03:31.931 --> 00:03:35.253
"No, I don't think so," he said.

69
00:03:35.273 --> 00:03:37.233
"Excuse me, I have to go."

70
00:03:37.974 --> 00:03:40.895
Suddenly Perda realized why he looked familiar.

71
00:03:41.535 --> 00:03:47.077
He resembled someone she'd met a couple of days earlier—the father of Mellis' friend.

72
00:03:47.097 --> 00:03:49.078
"Are you Anso?"

73
00:03:49.518 --> 00:03:50.019
she asked.

74
00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:51.679
The boy looked startled.

75
00:03:52.079 --> 00:03:53.260
"How do you know my name?"

76
00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:55.721
"I'm Perda," she said.

77
00:03:55.741 --> 00:03:57.362
"Mellis is my friend.

78
00:03:57.943 --> 00:03:59.044
I'm searching for her.

79
00:03:59.544 --> 00:04:00.585
Do you know where she is?"

80
00:04:00.605 --> 00:04:04.707
"Shh!" Anso glanced around.

81
00:04:05.208 --> 00:04:06.469
But there was nobody in sight.

82
00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:08.930
"Yes, I'm going there now."

83
00:04:09.551 --> 00:04:12.333
He showed Perda a loaf of bread hidden in his shirt.

84
00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:15.415
"Her new boss won't give her any food.

85
00:04:16.115 --> 00:04:19.758
He says she has to eat with the plonks she's taking care of."

86
00:04:19.778 --> 00:04:22.820
"Please bring me to her," Perda begged.

87
00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.042
"I need to see her so I can figure out how to rescue her.

88
00:04:26.542 --> 00:04:27.462
You can trust me.

89
00:04:27.843 --> 00:04:28.563
I promise!"

90
00:04:29.443 --> 00:04:32.985
Anso hesitated, and then nodded with a small smile.

91
00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:36.007
"Any friend of Mellis is a friend of mine.

92
00:04:36.807 --> 00:04:40.509
Come! We'll have to sneak past Trof, the owner of the farm.

93
00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.510
He's not a nice man."

94
00:04:43.331 --> 00:04:46.052
They headed down the road as quickly as Perda could shuffle.

95
00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:53.248
As they went, she told Anso everything that had happened since she and Zann had arrived in Terrica.

96
00:04:53.268 --> 00:04:58.710
Anso looked a bit skeptical when Perda said she came from another world, but he seemed willing to

97
00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.210
believe her.

98
00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:02.031
Finally Perda saw the farm.

99
00:05:02.771 --> 00:05:04.992
Anso led her into a grove of trees.

100
00:05:06.412 --> 00:05:09.693
They sneaked through them to the back fence of the farm.

101
00:05:11.433 --> 00:05:15.915
It was hard to climb the fence in shackles, but with Anso's help, Perda managed it.

102
00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:23.779
They crept across a dirty yard and into a pen where a dozen large, short-legged creatures snorted and

103
00:05:23.939 --> 00:05:27.081
squealed and fought each other for scraps of smelly food.

104
00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:30.284
"So those are plonks," Perda thought.

105
00:05:30.624 --> 00:05:32.766
And then she spotted something else.

106
00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:37.529
Perched on a barrel was a dirty and disheveled Mellis.

107
00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.212
Her face lit up when she saw Perda and Anso.

108
00:05:41.232 --> 00:05:43.274
"You came!"

109
00:05:43.794 --> 00:05:44.475
Mellis cried.

110
00:05:44.975 --> 00:05:46.056
She rushed toward them.

111
00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:52.454
Suddenly a young plonk dashed in front of her, its beady eyes fixed on a half-eaten vegetable.

112
00:05:53.154 --> 00:05:56.715
Mellis tripped over the animal, sending it tipping over into the muck.

113
00:05:57.335 --> 00:06:02.216
The plonk squealed loudly, and within seconds the rest of the plonks took up the cry.

114
00:06:02.236 --> 00:06:04.497
"Hey!" a man shouted.

115
00:06:04.517 --> 00:06:06.417
"What's going on out there?"

116
00:06:06.437 --> 00:06:08.818
"We have to hide!"

117
00:06:09.378 --> 00:06:10.618
Anso hissed in terror.

118
00:06:11.119 --> 00:06:16.040
But the sticky muck of the plonk pen made it even harder for Perda to move.

119
00:06:16.684 --> 00:06:22.214
Before she could hide, a large, mustached man with a ruddy face stomped into the pen.

120
00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:25.700
"Who dares to sneak onto my property?"

121
00:06:26.101 --> 00:06:28.706
he roared, grabbing Anso by the arm.
